Firmware: ODROID-C5 bootloader: Amlogic's boot stages (BL2 and the stages it
          loads, BL30, BL31 and BL32, signed and encrypted for the S905X5M)
          and Hardkernel's U-Boot (BL33), in one file, u-boot.bin.signed
Hardware: Hardkernel ODROID-C5 (Amlogic S905X5M, SoC family S7D)
Files:    the SD card's sectors from 1 (byte 512), written by the image
          build; the root file system has only the license texts below
          /usr/share/licenses/amlogic-s7d-bootloader and the manifest
Source:   Hardkernel's Yocto layer https://github.com/mdrjr/meta-odroid-aml,
          commit 548e2f037e01c626e3fc964fa298464df148fd51,
          recipes-bsp/u-boot-odroid-c5/files/u-boot.bin.signed (3379200
          bytes, SHA-256
          8c2e66919a05921d79e130cc00a977a07cf8df6b34153e66c18c3241c0809e3c)

Copyright Amlogic, Inc. (the boot stages BL2 to BL32)
Copyright the U-Boot authors and Hardkernel Co., Ltd. (U-Boot)

Terms:
- U-Boot is under the GNU General Public License version 2 (the text
  below); the layer's recipe (u-boot-odroid-c5.bb) states GPL-2.0-only.
  Its corresponding source is Hardkernel's: the submodule bl33/v2023 of
  the branch odroidc5-v2023.01 of https://github.com/hardkernel/u-boot
  (commit c99f3409d5cad031b365fd871e543f97af893f88), on
  https://git.odroid.com/yocto/uboot.  zedBSD changes nothing in it.
- Amlogic's boot stages: no licence text for them was found, in the layer,
  in Hardkernel's U-Boot tree or in the file.  For the boot stages of its
  other SoCs Amlogic's published terms (for example the LICENSE of
  https://github.com/LibreELEC/amlogic-boot-fip) say they are provided
  under a Software License Agreement with Amlogic and that redistribution
  and use, modified or not, are prohibited without Amlogic's prior written
  permission.  Whether those terms apply to this file is not known.  Use it
  only on your own ODROID-C5, and do not pass on an SD card image made with
  it until the terms are known.
- The boot ROM accepts only stages signed for the S905X5M, so the file is
  written as it is; zedBSD does not modify, re-sign or rebuild it.
